Ababa, ETHIOPIA Website: https://library.au.int Email: library@africa-union.org How do I contact the library? For General Library Matters Mr. Garoma Daba, Librarian Email: library@africa-union.org Tel: +251-115182326 ext 2326 For Queries Regarding Journals and other Periodicals Email: librarys@africa-union.org For Reference Queries Email: libraryc@africa-union.org Who can use the AUC Library? The AUC Library users are: Staff of the AUC and AU Member States Embassies in Addis Ababa Family members of Staff of the AUC and AU Member States Embassies in Addis Ababa AU Partners, Researchers from within and outside Africa working on African issues What are the Hours of Operations? The AUC Library is open from Monday to Friday during AU working hours: Morning: from 8:00 am to 1:00 pm Afternoon: from 2:00 pm to 5:00 pm The Library is closed during weekends and holidays observed by the African Union. AU Official Holidays - 2021 January 1 - International New Year January 7 - Ethiopian Christmas January 20 - Ethiopian Epiphany (Timket) March 2 - Victory of Adwa April 2 - International Good Friday April 30 - Ethiopian Good Friday May 1 - International Labour Day May 5 - Ethiopian Patriots Day May 13 - Eid Al Fitr Ramadan* May 25 - Africa Day May 28 - Overthrow of Dergue Regime July 20 - Eid Al Adha* September 9 - AU Day September 11 - Ethiopian New Year September 27 - Ethiopian Meskel (Finding of the True Cross) October 19 - Mawlid (Birth of the Prophet Mohamed) * December 25 - International Christmas * To be celebrated as announced by the local authorities at duty station Who can borrow materials? Currently only staff members of the AUC and AU Member States Embassies in Addis Ababa can borrow materials from the library. For AUC Staff, there is a one-time registration (see attached form) that needs to be filled and submitted with a copy of valid AU ID For Staff of AU Member States Embassies in Addis Ababa, there is also a one-time registration (see attached form) that needs to be filled and a guarantee letter (see attached sample) that should be submitted together with a valid picture ID. The letter should be submitted in a letter headed paper of the respective embassy and bear their official seal. Other users can use the AUC Library materials in-house. How can I borrow/renew a book? Registered Users may borrow up to 4 books/periodicals at a time for a period of 15 days. If they need additional time, they can renew by calling, emailing or visiting the library. The library has materials that cannot be borrowed at all (reference materials) and others may have shorter loan period like periodicals (magazines). Kindly inquire at one of the reference desks with Library Staff. How can I reserve a book? If a book you want to read is out on loan, you can reserve it by either visiting the library, or placing a call or sending an email with details of book to hold. How can I search for materials held by the AUC Library? To find books/journals/ journal articles, etc held in the AUC library collection, you can search our online catalogue through our website @ https://library.au.int How do I access electronic resources? The AUC Library subscribes to several electronic resources (journals and databases), which are available for AUC users only within AU premises. Users are able to access these e-resources either by using any desktop computer within the Library or AU compound or contact the library. For a list of available resources - currently subscribed journal titles go to https://library.au.int/glossary and for electronic libraries and/or databases visit the section of e-Library/databases. How to easily navigate through the website For ease of navigation and quick access, a sitemap of the library website is available at https://library.au.int/sitemap . Can children use the Library? The Library has a section for children books and space where they can read by respecting library rules and regulations. However, unaccompanied children below the age of 12 are not allowed into the Library. Can I bring something to eat/drink into the library? No, users are not allowed to consume Food and Drinks in the Library. Can I bring my stuff into the Library? Users can take their handbag, laptops and reading materials into the library. But, they have to leave their backpacks in the lockers provided by the entrance of the respective Reading Rooms. Can I recommend a book for purchase? Can I search the Library's catalogue from my office or home? Yes, the AUC library online catalogue is accessible from anywhere where you have internet access https://library.au.int African Union LIBRARY ©The AU Library, 2026 "Books are a Capital Resource. The more they are used, the more they add value into the lives of the readers...." Deputy Chairperson of the AUC, Feb. 2019 Library Hours Monday-Friday ( Mornings ): 8am-1pm Monday-Friday ( Afternoons ): 2pm-5pm Closed on Weekends and AU Officials Holidays* Links Contact us | Ask a Librarian FAQ | Sitemap | Help AU Home | AU Offices | Webmail fetchField() + $start_count;
